<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ApprovalProcess xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ApprovalProcess> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error. The rationale below lives in this comment
        rather than in <description> because a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the
        Metadata API. ⚠ DO NOT ASSUME THE 255-CHARACTER CAP that binds RecordType and
        ValidationRule descriptions applies here: the five approval files already in this repo
        carry descriptions of 442 to 617 characters (measured against git HEAD, 2026-08-19).
        The descriptions written in this change are nevertheless kept under 255, so the rule is
        uniform across every metadata type in this tranche and never has to be re-measured.

        NEW 2026-08-19. BOV_Submission__c had no approval process before this change.

        WHAT IT REPLACES AND WHY IT MOVED OBJECT. The on-market broker sign-off used to run on
        the DISPOSITION, as Disposition__c.Broker_Selection_Approval at stage BOV Outreach. It
        approves the SELECTED SUBMISSION now, because the submission is what the principals are
        actually deciding between: the approval page shows THIS broker's economics next to the
        approval history, instead of a Disposition record that names one broker in a lookup and
        hides the other four responses. Broker_Selection_Approval survives, repointed to the
        OFF-MARKET direct pick.

        🔴 THE RECORD-EDITABILITY ARGUMENT IS WHY THIS OBJECT PLACEMENT MATTERS, NOT JUST A
        PREFERENCE. recordEditability = AdminOnly locks the SUBMISSION while this approval is
        pending. The record the automation must write on approval is the PARENT Disposition,
        which is NOT locked - so BovSubmissionTriggerHandler updates the parent SYNCHRONOUSLY,
        allOrNone = false, SYSTEM mode, the same shape ContractExecutionService already uses.
        The three Disposition-target approvals cannot do that (they lock the very record they
        must advance), which is why THEY need the semaphore-plus-Queueable route and this one
        does not.

        ENTRY IS Submission_Status__c = 'Selected'. That is the team's pick, made in
        bovComparisonMatrix. It is deliberately NOT scoped by the parent's stage: submitting is
        driven by the Submit_Selected_Broker quick action, whose flexipage visibility rule and
        whose server-side gate in DispositionApprovalService both already require the parent to
        be at BOV Outreach. Duplicating that stage test here would make a cross-object entry
        criterion out of a check two other layers already perform correctly.

        ⚠ Approval_Status__c IS A SECOND, DISTINCT PICKLIST FROM Submission_Status__c on this
        object, and the trigger requires BOTH: Approved AND Selected. It also requires the parent
        to be CURRENTLY at BOV Outreach. That third guard is what makes a later broker
        replacement safe - BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker demotes the old submission
        to Backup and CLEARS its Approval_Status__c, and a replacement performed after the stage
        already advanced does NOT re-advance it.

        ⚠ REJECTION MOVES NOTHING. Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected records the outcome and the
        Disposition stays at BOV Outreach so a different submission can be selected and
        resubmitted.

        ⚠ FIELD-UPDATE NAMING. agent-output/design-requirements.md transcribed these as
        Set_BOV_Approval_* and flagged the spelling as open. Set_Broker_Approval_* was chosen, to
        match this process's own name and the business event. workflows/BOV_Submission__c
        .workflow-meta.xml uses the same spelling; those are the only two files that must agree.

        approvalPageFields carry only fields that DPEG_Disposition_View already grants read on -
        an approver who cannot read a field on the approval page sees a blank, not an error.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. workflows/BOV_Submission__c.workflow-meta.xml and
        objects/BOV_Submission__c/fields/Approval_Status__c.field-meta.xml must both land FIRST.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <allowRecall>true</allowRecall>
    <allowedSubmitters>
        <type>owner</type>
    </allowedSubmitters>
    <approvalPageFields>
        <field>Name</field>
        <field>Owner</field>
        <field>Property_Name__c</field>
        <field>Broker_Display__c</field>
        <field>BOV_Amount__c</field>
        <field>Cap_Rate__c</field>
        <field>Commission_Rate__c</field>
        <field>Days_To_Market__c</field>
        <field>Hist_Success_Rate__c</field>
        <field>Submission_Status__c</field>
    </approvalPageFields>
    <approvalStep>
        <allowDelegate>false</allowDelegate>
        <assignedApprover>
            <approver>
                <name>nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <approver>
                <name>aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@avanzasolutions.com</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <whenMultipleApprovers>FirstResponse</whenMultipleApprovers>
        </assignedApprover>
        <label>Principal Review</label>
        <name>Principal_Review_Step</name>
    </approvalStep>
    <description>ON-MARKET broker sign-off, on the selected BOV submission rather than the Disposition. Entry: Status is Selected. Approval sets Approval Status, which advances the parent Disposition from BOV Outreach to Broker Selection. See this file&apos;s XML comment.</description>
    <enableMobileDeviceAccess>false</enableMobileDeviceAccess>
    <entryCriteria>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>BOV_Submission__c.Submission_Status__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Selected</value>
        </criteriaItems>
    </entryCriteria>
    <finalApprovalActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Broker_Approval_Approved</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalApprovalActions>
    <finalApprovalRecordLock>false</finalApprovalRecordLock>
    <finalRejectionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalRejectionActions>
    <finalRejectionRecordLock>false</finalRejectionRecordLock>
    <label>Broker Finalize Approval</label>
    <processOrder>1</processOrder>
    <recordEditability>AdminOnly</recordEditability>
    <showApprovalHistory>true</showApprovalHistory>
</ApprovalProcess>
